> Question 1.  Once I beat the Mines and Sokoban (first time for either
> one, let alone both), the main dungeon got a LOT easier--the next
> 15-20 levels were a breeze.  Is this usually the case?

Often it is.  If you have excellent equipment (like DSM) it is not
hard to get deep into the game.

> Question 2.  I gave all my pocket change (the $140 I was carrying) to
> the Priestess of Gehennom in the Valley of the Dead, and she went
> berserk and killed me.  What gives?

When it comes to priests, the best gold to give is 400 times your
experience level.  (Which works, I believe, even with the VoD
priest.)  I'm not aware of priests getting angry when given less
money, but I haven't looked up in the source.  Priests who are asleep,
however, are known to get angry if you wake them up.

> Advice 1 (and Only).  Don't pick a fight with a Priest when you're XP
> level 7, unless you really know what you're doing.  (I didn't!)

Yeah, priests tend to be tough opponents.  It's generally a bad idea
to kill one yourself though, other than the High Priest(ess) of
Moloch, as it can result in losing valuable protection.

